                <head>112. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Presidential elections held on February 3, 1957, resulted in the election of
                        Luis A. Somoza as President of Nicaragua. Somoza defeated Edmundo Amador, the nominee of
                    the Nicaraguan Conservative Party. Documentation on this subject is in
                    Department of State, Central Files 717.00 and 717.11.</p>
            </div>
